-- a binding claim: this oriented molecule, that target, a measurement of the affinity with its event
-- and its warrant, and the proof that the measurement was of this molecule. The claim is about the
-- oriented molecule, not the bond graph, because the two enantiomers of a drug are two claims — which
-- thalidomide settled at the cost of about ten thousand children. The affinity is a natural number,
-- the pKi in hundredths, so the value type says which quantity it is and two kinds of measurement
-- cannot be aggregated by accident.
BindClaim : Type 1
BindClaim = (S : Oriented) × Prot × (m : Measured Nat) × (rep-mol Nat (meas-report Nat m) ≡ or-mol S)
